The bounded read-only inventory check is available as:

```sh
cargo run --locked -p games-build -- ledger check PATH BYTES ROWS
```

It verifies stable identity components, distinct caller/callee pairs,
recognized dispositions and the presence of evidence and Rust mappings
where required for completion claims. It reports aggregate counts,
not original function data, and does not certify semantic accuracy,
individual call sites or dynamic reachability. Synthetic tests cover
malformed identities, duplicate records, dangling or nonreciprocal
pairs, row bounds and missing implementation evidence. On the private
ledger it reported 788 functions, 25,803 owned instruction bytes,
2,893 distinct graph pairs, 686 discovered, 100 unresolved and two
non-runtime functions. No implemented function is claimed by that
check. The task remains open.

